# Issue #7 bench run on the Pi 5, 2026-11-19 UTC (the evening of 2026-11-18 local time). Branch issue-7-gwmon-v2 at ab08d87.
# The card was not reflashed. It holds the issue #4 image (a611da7) with the issue #6 files, plus four files from this
# branch's Buildroot build, copied over SSH; /etc/init.d/S60station was deleted by hand. SHA-256 on the Pi and inside
# the new rootfs.ext2 (sdcard.img 3115d14cf0883648f67360ab9aca2815778c71d9ebab93855153f93fa6a2b005):
#   192e8d24d283ceae55c83a33379b0bb2ed91055c3b6c8f1d5e0cd3e00a603523  /usr/bin/gwmon
#   ffdba9ea35f6ebc408583a7293121e50c613bef0d35ab57ae5221cfaa80ba2ff  /usr/bin/station-run.sh
#   89587a446dcca26366085d39fa31516362e1bebf989fce22541d3f2bb1598be2  /etc/init.d/S99gwmon
#   e310843dd8ecf632cb526b3e80888590511fcf6e6e35975ca0efac18bc8f2e14  /etc/station/station.conf
#   3d3ccb94aa342c1979aa7f045be6b8ad8e81e85ae2ada6687c7abceea56291cd  /usr/bin/station (unchanged since issue #4)
# After these tests the session link was added to the header comments (578707c). The image was built again and
# station-run.sh (b15fbe4b...c4d3), S99gwmon (bc0fb04b...26cf) and station.conf (130a0296...41f0) were copied to the Pi
# from that build. The gwmon binary is the same in both builds.
# 192.168.0.123 is the Pi and 192.168.0.107 the PC. Each section is the output of one small script run on the Pi over
# SSH as root; docs/issue7-gwmon-v2.md ("How to repeat the bench tests") has the commands. "Status line, read
# from the PC" is what `nc 192.168.0.123 9000` prints. In Station's log the account-specific endpoint IDs are replaced
# by <id>. Times in syslog and station.log are UTC.

